    "cutHeight": 0.55,
    "notes": "Pivots as kit_lib: a wall, doorway or cut piece has its origin at the centre of its base on the room-side face (the room is its local +z in game space; masonry behind it to z -0.4, and down to y -0.8 so sunk water never shows a gap); an 8 m cell edge is segment, doorway, segment (2 + 4 + 2 m) or four segments. Corner: origin on the room's inside corner, the room in its local +x/+z quadrant: NW rotationY 0, NE -90, SE 180, SW 90. Walls whose outer side faces the camera use the cut pieces. Floor tiles: 2 m, any quarter turn. floorAlt / wallAlt: [meshId, chance] per tile / full wall segment, never a wallAlt behind a wall-hung prop. doorways.trap is the Tide Gate trap skin (a lifting sluice gate)."
  },
  "water": {
    "knee": 0.45,
    "deep": -0.35,
    "kneeOpacity": 0.62,
    "note": "Pieces with \"water\": true carry slot-15 faces whose COLOR_0.A is their opacity (kit_lib keeps A = 1 elsewhere): knee-deep 0.62, deep 1, falling to 0 at soft edges (vlt_floor_water_edge, the pools of the breach, cage and chest, the wet tile's puddle). Draw them with a transparent water material (07: caustics scrolling on the knee-deep water, a fog volume on the deep). Knee-deep water is an overlay 0.45 m over the floor (the floor tile stays; characters standing at y 0 wade); deep water sits 0.35 m below the floor and its tile has a hole (the floor tile goes), lined by vlt_quay_edge_2m. The arena tides (07 §2.8) can move the knee-deep tiles up."
  },
